    "sentence_translations": [
      "When Do You Say “Sorry”?",
      "",
      "In China, you don’t often hear people say “dui bu qi”. Do Chinese people not like apologizing?",
      "This is not the case, because there are many ways to apologize in Chinese and “dui bu qi” is only one of them.",
      "",
      "“Dui bu qi” is a very formal and serious way to apologize.",
      "If you do something wrong that has a big impact on others, you must certainly sincerely say “dui bu qi”.",
      "Normally people will say “bao qian”.",
      "For example, if your colleagues invite you out to lunch but you don't have time, you can say “bao qian”.",
      "“Bu hao yisi” is the mildest way to apologize.",
      "If you are bothering someone for help, you can say “bu hao yisi”.",
      "For example, when you ask a stranger for directions, or you want to ask someone to help you take a picture.",
      "If you want to pass through a crowd, you can say: “Bu hao yisi, please let me pass.”"
    ]
  }
